WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.278 --> 00:00:01.810
- Hey everybody this is Gary Vaynerchuk,

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:03.835
and this is #podSessions.

00:00:03.835 --> 00:00:06.803
Pretty much my favorite
pillar type that I've created

00:00:06.803 --> 00:00:08.836
in the last year or two,

00:00:08.836 --> 00:00:10.010
but I don't get to do often,

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:14.067
'cause you know first I like
mixing up the guests I have,

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:15.619
the format if you're listening

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:18.389
or watching for the first
time is three guests and I.

00:00:18.389 --> 00:00:19.924
And we just kinda shoot the shit,

00:00:19.924 --> 00:00:21.228
talk about different stuff,

00:00:21.228 --> 00:00:22.741
people that I have context for,

00:00:22.741 --> 00:00:24.757
either I'm watching
very carefully from afar

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:25.774
or actually know.

00:00:25.774 --> 00:00:28.548
All three here, I
actually know pretty well,

00:00:28.548 --> 00:00:30.685
two I've met several times
in person, and one I've,

00:00:30.685 --> 00:00:33.125
I've interacted with
you the most actually,

00:00:33.125 --> 00:00:35.775
but we haven't met, and I'm
glad we finally did that.

00:00:35.775 --> 00:00:37.357
And so I'm gonna let them
introduce themselves,

00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:40.766
one minute bio-stories,
who they are, what they do,

00:00:40.766 --> 00:00:42.550
and maybe a little fun fact,

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.790
and then we're gonna get into the show

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.055
and I'm gonna talk about some topics

00:00:45.055 --> 00:00:48.160
and then also interject my
context of why I love them,

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.383
or admire them, or am curious about them,

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.655
or maybe dislike them.

00:00:51.655 --> 00:00:53.487
I might be sand-baggin'
somebody right now, who knows.

00:00:53.487 --> 00:00:57.552
But why don't we start with
the lady to my left first.

00:00:57.552 --> 00:00:59.276
- Alright, I'm Erika Nardini.

00:00:59.276 --> 00:01:00.884
I'm the CEO of Barstool Sports.

00:01:00.884 --> 00:01:03.157
I've been at Barstool for two years.

00:01:03.157 --> 00:01:04.533
We've taken the company

00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:08.141
from 12 people and very small investment

00:01:08.141 --> 00:01:10.765
to over a hundred million
dollar evaluation,

00:01:10.765 --> 00:01:13.846
and we're becoming a
juggernaut in the men's space.

00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:16.392
Prior to that I had a
company called Backstage,

00:01:16.392 --> 00:01:19.832
where I really sought
to connect music artists

00:01:19.832 --> 00:01:21.136
and their fans directly.

00:01:21.136 --> 00:01:24.361
I hate disintermediation
and I thought that artists

00:01:24.361 --> 00:01:27.901
should be able to own their
data, connect with their fans,

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:30.993
have an LTV type
relationship, and ultimately--

00:01:30.993 --> 00:01:32.344
- Lifetime value for all the kids at home.

00:01:32.344 --> 00:01:33.177
- Yep, yep.

00:01:33.177 --> 00:01:35.246
And ultimately to be
able to know your fans

00:01:35.246 --> 00:01:37.286
and connect with them
directly which is something

00:01:37.286 --> 00:01:39.445
I've always been really passionate about.

00:01:39.445 --> 00:01:41.813
Was the CMO of AOL, worked at a bunch

00:01:41.813 --> 00:01:43.782
of big digital media companies,

00:01:43.782 --> 00:01:45.639
started my career thinking
I was gonna be a lawyer,

00:01:45.639 --> 00:01:47.303
which definitely did not happen.

00:01:47.303 --> 00:01:48.136
- Now did you,

00:01:48.136 --> 00:01:50.207
when you tell people
you're the CEO of Barstool,

00:01:50.207 --> 00:01:53.736
which is known for not only
being a young male brand,

00:01:53.736 --> 00:01:54.569
but like--

00:01:54.569 --> 00:01:55.432
Edgy.

00:01:55.432 --> 00:01:57.416
- Yeah, like it's like
the only thing out there

00:01:57.416 --> 00:01:58.712
that I feel like, oh I could,

00:01:58.712 --> 00:02:00.379
like it's real edgy.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:02.143
- Yeah.

00:02:02.143 --> 00:02:02.976
- Like are people like,

00:02:02.976 --> 00:02:04.061
"Get the fuck out here" when you say it?

00:02:04.061 --> 00:02:04.894
Do some people actually think--

00:02:04.894 --> 00:02:05.776
- Yeah it's shocking.

00:02:05.776 --> 00:02:07.622
- Like if you're just
hanging out in real life,

00:02:07.622 --> 00:02:09.495
do some people actually
think you're joking,

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:10.846
and making a joke, and then they're like,

00:02:10.846 --> 00:02:12.019
"No really, but what?"

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:12.852
- Yeah.

00:02:12.852 --> 00:02:13.685
- I would believe that.

00:02:13.685 --> 00:02:14.917
Like if I didn't know you and know how,

00:02:14.917 --> 00:02:17.271
and like really know how badass you are,

00:02:17.271 --> 00:02:19.693
but also just know that you were,

00:02:19.693 --> 00:02:21.511
and I was like at a dinner conference

00:02:21.511 --> 00:02:22.550
and everyone went around.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.406
I'd be like, oh that's funny.

00:02:24.406 --> 00:02:25.372
- That's funny yeah.

00:02:25.372 --> 00:02:29.196
I think I'm a curiosity
in the whole mix of it,

00:02:29.196 --> 00:02:31.076
because people wouldn't expect a woman

00:02:31.076 --> 00:02:32.532
to be a CEO of Barstool.

00:02:32.532 --> 00:02:34.804
I love Barstool, I'm
super proud to work there,

00:02:34.804 --> 00:02:36.741
was a huge fan of Barstool.

00:02:36.741 --> 00:02:39.073
Built a lot of Backstage
based on Barstool,

00:02:39.073 --> 00:02:39.906
to be honest with you.

00:02:39.906 --> 00:02:41.092
- Because you know the underlining truth,

00:02:41.092 --> 00:02:42.971
not the kind of like,

00:02:42.971 --> 00:02:45.159
the makeup that people get upset about.

00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:47.118
Whether somebody curses or is raunchy.

00:02:47.118 --> 00:02:49.858
- I think we live in an outrage society.

00:02:49.858 --> 00:02:53.448
I think the pressure to be PC is just--

00:02:53.448 --> 00:02:54.281
- [Gary] Overwhelming.

00:02:54.281 --> 00:02:55.114
- Overwhelming.

00:02:55.114 --> 00:02:56.730
And it's strangling.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.566
- Understood.

00:02:57.566 --> 00:02:59.842
- And the judgment that
comes with that is punitive.

00:02:59.842 --> 00:03:02.166
And we are an agenda-less brand

00:03:02.166 --> 00:03:04.555
that just cares about
making its audience laugh.

00:03:04.555 --> 00:03:06.733
And we intimately get that audience.

00:03:06.733 --> 00:03:08.762
That's what I love about it.

00:03:08.762 --> 00:03:09.613
- Thanks for doing this.

00:03:09.613 --> 00:03:10.446
- [Erika] Thank you.

00:03:10.446 --> 00:03:11.279
- Go ahead, my man.

00:03:11.279 --> 00:03:12.287
- My name's Reezy.

00:03:12.287 --> 00:03:14.490
