00:04:21.795 --> 00:04:23.379
I dropped outta highschool in 10th grade.

00:04:23.379 --> 00:04:25.164
Had a kid, got married when I was 16.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.523
Still married 18 years later.

00:04:27.523 --> 00:04:32.523
13 years ago I found out
about selling books on Amazon.

00:04:32.891 --> 00:04:34.372
And within a year--

00:04:34.372 --> 00:04:35.828
- How?

00:04:35.828 --> 00:04:36.990
Somebody said something somewhere?

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.076
- I was already into
Ebay because they were

00:04:39.076 --> 00:04:41.444
running commercials on
TV when I was like 14.

00:04:41.444 --> 00:04:43.188
So I sold everything I could,

00:04:43.188 --> 00:04:44.325
and I was an avid reader.

00:04:44.325 --> 00:04:47.141
One day I sold my Star
Wars books that I read.

00:04:47.141 --> 00:04:49.134
And they went for, I
started them for a penny,

00:04:49.134 --> 00:04:51.605
and they went for like
80% of the retail value,

00:04:51.605 --> 00:04:53.030
which blew my mind.

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:55.190
Later on in life, I was in thrift stores,

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.966
I seen people with barcode
scanners scanning books.

00:04:57.966 --> 00:04:59.470
I would ask them what are they doing.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:03.063
They would clam up and they
would act like I was invisible.

00:05:03.063 --> 00:05:04.863
Imagine an adult acting
like you're invisible.

00:05:04.863 --> 00:05:07.231
So I was like oh they're
making a lot of fucking money.

00:05:07.231 --> 00:05:08.064
(laughing)

00:05:08.064 --> 00:05:09.360
And I'm technology minded.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.193
They had barcode scanners.

00:05:10.193 --> 00:05:11.058
- For all the people out there,

00:05:11.058 --> 00:05:13.994
that's called street smarts.

00:05:13.994 --> 00:05:15.778
Some of the things they
don't teach you in school

00:05:15.778 --> 00:05:18.058
is when somebody clams up it's because

00:05:18.058 --> 00:05:19.690
they're making a lot of money.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:20.523
Keep going, my man.

00:05:20.523 --> 00:05:21.356
Reezy.

00:05:21.356 --> 00:05:22.739
- So they had a barcode
scanner and I was like

00:05:22.739 --> 00:05:25.051
oh those are at least $100 to $300 bucks,

00:05:25.051 --> 00:05:26.659
so they gotta be making some money.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:27.723
So I drilled into it.

00:05:27.723 --> 00:05:29.060
YouTube wasn't out yet, the iPhone--

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:29.994
- Hold on, that just made me smile.

00:05:29.994 --> 00:05:31.122
Hold on, I gotta stop you,

00:05:31.122 --> 00:05:32.202
'cause that just makes me smile, too.

00:05:32.202 --> 00:05:34.627
Just thinking about your
psychology at that point.

00:05:34.627 --> 00:05:37.091
Be like, "Yo, they're really on,

00:05:37.091 --> 00:05:38.219
"because they got the barcode,"

00:05:38.219 --> 00:05:40.107
you know, that's amazing.

00:05:40.107 --> 00:05:40.940
Keep going.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.380
- So smartphones weren't out yet.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:43.315
iPhone wasn't out yet.

00:05:43.315 --> 00:05:45.756
YouTube wasn't out yet.

00:05:45.756 --> 00:05:47.116
There was no Reezy Resells.

00:05:47.116 --> 00:05:48.436
There was no books I could read.

00:05:48.436 --> 00:05:52.229
I exhausted my Google-fu trying
to figure out what it was.

00:05:52.229 --> 00:05:55.093
And I couldn't figure out how
